   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.2,
   "chunks": [
    "Who really profits",
    "from war?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 2.31,
   "chunks": [
    "This is the",
    "military-industrial complex.",
    "And you see, a president",
    "warned us about it in 1961.",
    "A general, no less."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 10.12,
   "chunks": [
    "Dwight Eisenhower.",
    "Five-star general.",
    "His farewell warning?",
    "Guard against unwarranted influence,",
    "by the military-industrial complex."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 18.34,
   "chunks": [
    "Where did it start?",
    "World War Two.",
    "Car plants built bombers.",
    "Willow Run:",
    "one B-24 an hour."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 24.2,
   "chunks": [
    "Then the Cold War arms race.",
    "Its spin-offs?",
    "Jet engines. Satellites.",
    "GPS.",
    "ARPANET, the internet's ancestor."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 31.67,
   "chunks": [
    "Today?",
    "World military spending:",
    "$2.9 trillion.",
    "A record, says SIPRI."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 36.95,
   "chunks": [
    "Who gets the contracts?",
    "The top 100 arms makers:",
    "$679 billion.",
    "Lockheed Martin leads."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 43.65,
   "chunks": [
    "Now explode one fighter jet.",
    "Engine. Radar.",
    "Wings. Chips.",
    "The F-35 alone?",
    "Over 1,900 suppliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 51.32,
   "chunks": [
    "And the climate?",
    "Militaries: maybe 5.5%",
    "of global emissions.",
    "An estimate.",
    "Reporting is voluntary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 58.43,
   "chunks": [
    "The new race?",
    "Drones and AI.",
    "Ukraine built about",
    "4 million drones in 2025."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 64.2,
   "chunks": [
    "Of course, the same machine",
    "also built GPS and the internet.",
    "Eisenhower's question still stands:",
    "who's steering it?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v12",
   "t": 71.25,
   "chunks": [
